### Rationale
H50 gate result: the Toeplitz tcgen05 conv works and is correct, but it misses both success lines. The row-shift and T-construction risks are solved, and the precision forms are simulated. It does not reach ≤100 µs at 64,96 or ≤25 µs at 32,128. The best rented times are 155 µs and 57.8 µs.

The cause was measured. A Toeplitz MMA with N=112 reads 7.5 KB of shared-memory operands per 60 clk, about 125 B/clk, which uses nearly the whole shared-memory port. Any other traffic in the same SM (staging writes, conversion, epilogue) slows it to 98–120 clk per MMA. On its own the MMA runs at 60 clk, close to ideal.

The 64,96 refutation line (>180 µs) did not fire. Per the brief, the archived solution is the r0 anchor with the probe kernel kept behind `#if 0`. It compiles with 0 B local (no stack), passes run_tests 16/16, and ships nothing to the merge.

